1
00:00:16,510 --> 00:00:41,480
 Stars, galaxy, in astral seas above, on cosmic paths we'll trace, man over wings.

2
00:01:28,950 --> 00:02:03,820
 Liberty is such a wandering thing, behind us all, come see, come take your place, we're leaving soon for-

3
00:02:03,820 --> 00:02:14,610
 End it, already.

4
00:03:30,520 --> 00:03:46,480
 Protection shield is invulnerable, ultimate weapon and we-

5
00:03:46,480 --> 00:03:52,820
 Calling all delegates, meeting at once in the General Assembly.

6
00:03:52,820 --> 00:03:56,990
 I repeat, an immediate session of the council, number one priority.

7
00:04:01,670 --> 00:04:03,630
 See and go on my observation screen.

8
00:04:03,710 --> 00:04:04,390
 A large object.

9
00:04:04,570 --> 00:04:05,890
 It could be an enormous spaceship.

10
00:04:06,400 --> 00:04:09,560
 One thing is certain, there are dozens of fighter craft accompanying it.

11
00:04:10,840 --> 00:04:13,450
 Yeah, I wonder.

12
00:04:14,620 --> 00:04:16,690
 Well, Lieutenant, how are you doing?

13
00:04:16,910 --> 00:04:18,010
 Are you feeling better?

14
00:04:18,510 --> 00:04:19,720
 Yes, thanks, Pierrot.

15
00:04:19,900 --> 00:04:21,250
 Only I still feel very weak.

16
00:04:21,580 --> 00:04:22,720
 You should get some sleep.

17
00:04:22,890 --> 00:04:24,130
 I'll give you a little sedative.

18
00:04:24,600 --> 00:04:26,220
 No, Pierrot, I don't think so.

19
00:04:26,460 --> 00:04:27,100
 I'm worried.

20
00:04:27,440 --> 00:04:29,500
 The feeling there's something terribly wrong.

21
00:04:29,500 --> 00:04:32,180
 Hey, you two, don't you think it's time we called?

22
00:04:32,340 --> 00:04:33,950
 We're okay and we should tell him.

23
00:04:35,260 --> 00:04:36,200
 Yes, I'll call Omega.

24
00:04:36,720 --> 00:04:38,370
 It's a crazy situation.

25
00:04:38,670 --> 00:04:41,360
 It is worrying. Who are these guys, anyway?

26
00:04:41,680 --> 00:04:44,270
 These humanoids who are after us. I'll call base.

27
00:04:45,330 --> 00:04:47,070
 Omega Control, go ahead.

28
00:04:47,510 --> 00:04:50,640
 This is Lieutenant Pierrot. Put on Colonel Pierre. It's urgent.

29
00:04:50,980 --> 00:04:52,610
 Negative. The colonel is in conference.

30
00:04:53,090 --> 00:04:54,550
 Well, then give me the commander.

31
00:04:55,180 --> 00:04:57,000
 Negative. Commander is in conference.

32
00:04:57,790 --> 00:05:00,770
 There's something wrong. An emergency session.

33
00:05:01,840 --> 00:05:04,120
 Give me Madam President. It's personal.

34
00:05:04,830 --> 00:05:08,820
 Negative, Lieutenant. The president is chairing the meeting. Impossible to disturb her.

35
00:05:08,820 --> 00:05:10,670
 Listen, it's top priority.

36
00:05:11,050 --> 00:05:12,030
 Lieutenant, I can't.

37
00:05:12,290 --> 00:05:15,390
 Okay, I want you to inform all three that I am calling.

38
00:05:15,670 --> 00:05:16,610
 Go ahead, I'll wait.

39
00:05:16,810 --> 00:05:19,170
 I can feel it. Something is really wrong.

40
00:05:29,800 --> 00:05:34,820
 Time is passing, gentlemen. We haven't much left.

41
00:05:35,340 --> 00:05:38,840
 What do you propose? Has anyone a suggestion?

42
00:05:39,780 --> 00:05:42,870
 What does the intergalactic police say?

43
00:05:43,280 --> 00:05:47,210
 The commander has just been to the calculation center. Here is his report.

44
00:05:47,210 --> 00:05:50,420
 The distance and trajectory are such that none of our ships

45
00:05:50,420 --> 00:05:52,680
 is in a position to intercept their craft and destroy it.

46
00:05:52,960 --> 00:05:55,480
 May I make that clear? We have no way to destroy it.

47
00:05:55,660 --> 00:05:58,200
 We do have allies who are quite close to the Earth.

48
00:05:58,400 --> 00:06:03,370
 Even the ones on Sirius and Barnard would have to come out of hyperspace, well before the solar system.

49
00:06:03,850 --> 00:06:05,430
 They would be too late to stop it.

50
00:06:07,400 --> 00:06:11,770
 Here is the estimated time for their operation as our computer service has worked it out.

51
00:06:12,190 --> 00:06:17,010
 Their device is at present at this location, just passing the region of Uranus.

52
00:06:17,010 --> 00:06:29,530
 Its path will take it past Saturn's orbit at 1340, then Jupiter's at 1425, the asteroid belt at 1440, Mars at 1455, hitting the Earth at precisely 15 hours.

53
00:06:30,840 --> 00:06:38,810
 According to our calculations, their base, or whatever, their control center is certainly in this region, no doubt patrolling this sector.

54
00:06:39,120 --> 00:06:46,560
 However, even if we were able to locate that control center and destroy it, which is in fact not likely, it would in no way help us to solve the problem in hand.

55
00:06:46,970 --> 00:06:50,020
 The prospect of complete destruction now menaces the Earth.

56
00:06:50,020 --> 00:07:00,690
 Tried sending a suicide mission of a great number of ships out of the Centaurus system that would take the risk of penetrating the solar system at hyperspace speed?

57
00:07:00,990 --> 00:07:04,950
 Coming out of hyperspace as close to the enemy craft as possible, would it work?

58
00:07:06,150 --> 00:07:08,150
 Hmm. Well, let's see.

59
00:07:08,390 --> 00:07:10,670
 Very little chance, none really.

60
00:07:10,850 --> 00:07:14,270
 More than nine-tenths of our craft would be destroyed before coming out of HS.

61
00:07:14,960 --> 00:07:18,230
 And even if a few did make it, the slightest error in calculation

62
00:07:18,230 --> 00:07:21,510
 would render any chance of catching it highly improbable.

63
00:07:21,970 --> 00:07:23,970
 If hyperspeed exit isn't perfect, it's useless.

64
00:07:23,970 --> 00:07:25,710
 It's useless anyway. It's going too fast.

65
00:07:25,710 --> 00:07:28,870
 In view of the fact that any other possibilities are excluded,

66
00:07:29,050 --> 00:07:31,070
 surely it's worth trying our only alternative.

67
00:07:31,580 --> 00:07:33,760
 No, no, I assure you the idea just wouldn't work.

68
00:07:34,180 --> 00:07:35,820
 We must not delude ourselves.

69
00:07:35,980 --> 00:07:37,460
 Note that the operation is well planned,

70
00:07:37,520 --> 00:07:40,060
 and according to photographs, their bomb is invulnerable.

71
00:07:40,810 --> 00:07:43,670
 Now, there's one slim chance, but it's very slim indeed.

72
00:07:44,160 --> 00:07:44,480
 Yes.

73
00:07:46,770 --> 00:07:50,660
 Go on board the thing and disarm it.

74
00:07:51,080 --> 00:07:52,210
 Well, that's insane.

75
00:07:52,710 --> 00:07:54,460
 Can you make such statements?

76
00:07:54,480 --> 00:07:55,460
 He lives in a dream.

77
00:07:55,540 --> 00:07:57,360
 How can he make jokes at such a time?

78
00:07:57,480 --> 00:07:58,460
 Can't you be serious?

79
00:07:59,710 --> 00:08:01,880
 All right, I'll be right there.

80
00:08:05,800 --> 00:08:15,830
 That's it.

81
00:08:15,990 --> 00:08:18,890
 If we have any one of our craft in the region of Earth,

82
00:08:18,890 --> 00:08:22,390
 We can then get aboard, and very quickly, we can disarm the rocket ship.

83
00:08:22,680 --> 00:08:23,990
 I don't know exactly how.

84
00:08:24,680 --> 00:08:28,850
 Our photographs from Titania aren't too clear, but we will have other photographs very soon.

85
00:08:29,510 --> 00:08:33,750
 Of course, we would need someone in the vicinity, and we have none, right, Colonel?

86
00:08:34,480 --> 00:08:40,270
 As it happens, in that region, there is a ship, a Hummingbird.

87
00:08:40,530 --> 00:08:42,330
 In that case, you get in contact.

88
00:08:43,130 --> 00:08:44,540
 What advice be, Colonel?

89
00:08:45,310 --> 00:08:49,520
 Captain, contact that Hummingbird. Top priority.

90
00:08:50,030 --> 00:08:51,390
 Yes, sir. At once, Colonel.

91
00:08:52,500 --> 00:08:53,980
 Hummingbird calling Hummingbird.

92
00:08:53,980 --> 00:08:56,880
 This is Omega Control calling Hummingbird.

93
00:08:57,120 --> 00:08:59,950
 This is Omega Control. Come in, Lieutenant.

94
00:09:00,400 --> 00:09:03,000
 Keep trying, Captain. It's urgent. Don't give up.

95
00:09:03,460 --> 00:09:06,620
 As soon as you get through to Lieutenant Pierrot, I want to talk to him.

96
00:09:11,170 --> 00:09:19,760
 What's wrong? I've lost contact completely.

97
00:09:20,110 --> 00:09:21,740
 Close to this little orange balloon.

98
00:09:22,260 --> 00:09:24,510
 Even if they tried calling, we wouldn't hear them.

99
00:09:24,770 --> 00:09:26,130
 Yeah, don't forget the interference.

100
00:09:26,530 --> 00:09:30,150
 We decided to stay a good distance from Saturn and its satellites for a good reason.

101
00:09:30,610 --> 00:09:33,760
 I know. You want to take a look at what I see here?

102
00:09:37,590 --> 00:09:40,930
 Fifteen minutes on a course to the right, we'll be out of the zone of vulnerability.

103
00:09:40,930 --> 00:09:42,710
 We'll program a little hyperspace.

104
00:09:43,120 --> 00:09:45,650
 And quick as a wink, we're on our way home, no problem.

105
00:09:51,180 --> 00:09:57,820
 Omega Control. Come in, Lieutenant. Come in.

106
00:09:58,750 --> 00:10:03,780
 Well, you see, there are limitations on possible ways of boarding the enemy ship.

107
00:10:03,880 --> 00:10:05,740
 I'll give you more details on that later.

108
00:10:06,270 --> 00:10:10,170
 When we've had a chance to look at the video pictures transmitted from Rhea,

109
00:10:10,470 --> 00:10:14,910
 analyze them, they may allow me to suggest a suitable approach, a vector angle.

110
00:10:15,500 --> 00:10:19,700
 Maestro, no, wait. Their craft is calculated to approach Saturn in about an hour.

111
00:10:19,700 --> 00:10:26,000
 And 25 minutes before the ultimatum expires.

112
00:10:26,510 --> 00:10:28,350
 And what would you suggest we do?

113
00:10:28,980 --> 00:10:31,780
 Shouldn't we warn Earth they're in danger?

114
00:10:32,000 --> 00:10:32,280
 Yes.

115
00:10:32,660 --> 00:10:34,370
 But before throwing them into panic,

116
00:10:34,730 --> 00:10:37,610
 we ought to be able to hold out some hope to our earthly friends.

117
00:10:37,930 --> 00:10:39,850
 We can't simply send them their death warrant.

118
00:10:40,150 --> 00:10:41,930
 And the Lunar Defense Base?

119
00:10:42,210 --> 00:10:45,550
 Couldn't it use its considerable power to create a wall of fire?

120
00:10:45,670 --> 00:10:48,630
 As I understand that the Lunar Base has sophisticated weapons.

121
00:10:49,030 --> 00:10:51,550
 The moon, well, it's less than two seconds from the target.

122
00:10:51,550 --> 00:10:56,250
 Once within its action perimeter, it will execute its mission, namely exploding.

123
00:10:56,710 --> 00:11:00,410
 But even if it happens in that vicinity, it will create considerable devastation.

124
00:11:01,440 --> 00:11:01,920
 Considerable.

125
00:11:02,340 --> 00:11:03,000
 No, no, no.

126
00:11:03,000 --> 00:11:04,960
 Let us consider other alternatives.

127
00:11:05,810 --> 00:11:10,880
 In any case, my friends, the craft's protection shield will allow it to resist any frontal attack.

128
00:11:10,980 --> 00:11:11,640
 Let's accept that.

129
00:11:12,030 --> 00:11:13,890
 So I can say that we are all agreed.

130
00:11:14,480 --> 00:11:16,580
 No one here wishes to surrender.

131
00:11:17,150 --> 00:11:18,560
 Oh, no question of that.

132
00:11:18,720 --> 00:11:19,940
 Absolutely no surrender.

133
00:11:19,940 --> 00:11:21,620
 We will never give in to aggression.

134
00:11:21,820 --> 00:11:22,740
 It's against our principles.

135
00:11:23,260 --> 00:11:25,960
 And so far my galaxy is concerned, there can be no doubt.

136
00:11:26,180 --> 00:11:29,260
 We intend to defend all our rights regardless of who threatens us.

137
00:11:29,640 --> 00:11:32,680
 Civilized beings must live in dignity, and for that we will fight.

138
00:11:33,000 --> 00:11:33,920
 Yes, I agree.

139
00:11:34,490 --> 00:11:37,210
 General Grouchley is a dangerous mad genius.

140
00:11:38,480 --> 00:11:42,220
 His terror would know no limits were he to be victorious now.

141
00:11:42,500 --> 00:11:46,640
 The General thinks anyone not with him is aggressively against him.

142
00:11:47,600 --> 00:11:49,740
 History is full of power mad dictators.

143
00:11:49,740 --> 00:11:52,600
 It's just as crazy as Grouchley, perhaps even crazier.

144
00:11:52,740 --> 00:11:55,540
 Calicula, Nero, Hitler, he was a bad one.

145
00:11:55,800 --> 00:11:58,740
 Their madness only helped them in their ambition for conquest.

146
00:11:59,000 --> 00:12:01,980
 Psychologically speaking, the origins of this average...

147
00:12:01,980 --> 00:12:02,900
 Well, it's not the moment.

148
00:12:03,520 --> 00:12:05,220
 Well, to go on, gentlemen, do go on.

149
00:12:05,520 --> 00:12:09,880
 It is imperative to find out whether Cassiopeia has more than this one bomb.

150
00:12:10,230 --> 00:12:13,070
 I believe it's unlikely, so we need only to use this one.

151
00:12:14,090 --> 00:12:16,790
 Hummingbird, hummingbird, this is Omega Control.

152
00:12:17,250 --> 00:12:18,090
 Come in, Lieutenant.

153
00:12:18,740 --> 00:12:20,900
 Omega Control calling hummingbird.

154
00:12:21,220 --> 00:12:22,140
 Come in at once, over.

155
00:12:25,230 --> 00:12:34,200
 Okay, kids, this is it. Going into hyperspace.

156
00:12:34,650 --> 00:12:37,090
 Wait a second. Hold it, Peter.

157
00:12:37,090 --> 00:12:45,410
 hummingbird calling hummingbird this is omega control this is hummingbird lieutenant piero go

158
00:12:45,410 --> 00:12:52,410
 ahead at last what's your position urgent request i'm putting you through to the colonel yes colonel

159
00:12:52,410 --> 00:12:57,130
 i understand what you said i know what the mission is but colonel i'll carry out your orders but i

160
00:12:57,130 --> 00:13:01,690
 think there's something that you should absolutely knows lieutenant listen to me there's no time to

161
00:13:01,690 --> 00:13:07,440
 lose now you will immediately carry out your orders program your craft as instructed now but

162
00:13:07,440 --> 00:13:09,980
 Colonel, you will execute your orders, Lieutenant.

163
00:13:10,460 --> 00:13:14,960
 In less than 30 minutes, he will be in the region of Saturn heading toward the sun.

164
00:13:15,340 --> 00:13:17,650
 He will be 20 minutes ahead of the rocket ship.

165
00:13:18,130 --> 00:13:19,730
 Let's hope he makes it in time.

166
00:13:35,580 --> 00:13:45,270
 Following your orders, I have programmed our trajectory as instructed.

167
00:13:45,530 --> 00:13:50,710
 But as I tried to tell you, we will very likely be detected by enemy fighter craft based on Mimas near Saturn.

168
00:13:51,490 --> 00:13:54,910
 And we may even encounter a much larger prize.

169
00:13:55,300 --> 00:13:56,810
 Any further instructions, Colonel?

170
00:13:57,410 --> 00:13:59,750
 Change course immediately toward Jupiter.

171
00:14:00,390 --> 00:14:03,130
 We will calculate a new trajectory for you.

172
00:14:03,130 --> 00:14:03,730
 Stand by.

173
00:14:05,840 --> 00:14:09,400
 Work out all possible paths of intersection on the Saturn-Jupiter axis.

174
00:14:11,270 --> 00:14:20,630
 This is the fastest one, and we need all the time we can get.

175
00:14:21,210 --> 00:14:22,660
 This one is safer.

176
00:14:24,800 --> 00:14:26,080
 Hummingbird, do you read me?

177
00:14:26,570 --> 00:14:27,230
 Yes, Colonel.

178
00:14:27,890 --> 00:14:29,710
 Okay, these are your instructions.

179
00:14:30,010 --> 00:14:33,170
 You will maneuver in order to circle Jupiter on the right.

180
00:14:33,580 --> 00:14:36,720
 Taking maximum advantage of all the cover the planet can provide,

181
00:14:36,980 --> 00:14:39,680
 you will intercept rocket ship as soon as it clears the planet.

182
00:14:39,680 --> 00:14:41,000
 You maintain the same axis.

183
00:14:41,480 --> 00:14:44,940
 This procedure will cost us time, but the safety of all of you is worth the price.

184
00:14:45,640 --> 00:14:46,960
 Carry out your maneuver, Lieutenant.

185
00:14:47,520 --> 00:14:50,090
 Must succeed. You're our only hope.

186
00:14:50,700 --> 00:14:52,580
 Radio contact in 15 minutes. Out.

187
00:14:53,600 --> 00:15:12,530
 I swear they will make contact at 14 hours 30.

188
00:15:13,170 --> 00:15:17,090
 The distance they have to travel now is only slightly shorter than that of the rocket.

189
00:15:17,370 --> 00:15:21,380
 Got to trust our kids. Now we have no choice.

190
00:15:22,050 --> 00:15:27,230
 I'd better give a little thought now to how these young people are going to get inside that darn thing once aboard it.

191
00:15:27,610 --> 00:15:29,310
 No need to... I don't know.

192
00:15:30,110 --> 00:15:34,920
 What we need is high-resolution pictures. These are so fuzzy that they're... I can't see a thing on them.

193
00:15:34,920 --> 00:15:36,480
 They're fuzzy as my beard.

194
00:15:37,280 --> 00:15:41,910
 Maneuver carried out successfully. Colonel, Saturn's orbital axis is behind us. All is ready.

195
00:15:42,400 --> 00:15:47,010
 Well done, son. You're still a little ahead of the rocket, but your trajectory is a bit longer.

196
00:15:47,690 --> 00:15:51,030
 For the record, Lieutenant, I'd like to say I'm sorry I didn't listen to you earlier.

197
00:15:51,370 --> 00:15:52,390
 We'd have gained precious time.

198
00:15:52,630 --> 00:15:53,410
 Piero! Piero!

199
00:15:53,710 --> 00:15:59,290
 In less than half an hour, we'll have analyzed the new pictures that we'll be getting from our Saturn relay station on Rhea.

200
00:15:59,290 --> 00:16:03,110
 At that time, I'll give you precise approach angle. Courage.

201
00:16:09,310 --> 00:16:31,690
 According to plan, General. Have you any news?

202
00:16:37,090 --> 00:16:38,170
 Discussion. I know him.

203
00:16:38,690 --> 00:16:41,150
 Believe me, democracies are great time wasters.

204
00:16:41,440 --> 00:16:44,640
 At the last minute, they'll hand us their surrender on a silver platter.

205
00:16:48,740 --> 00:16:57,880
 Good demonstration of their protection shield in action under a sustained attack.

206
00:16:57,980 --> 00:16:58,680
 You see what happens.

207
00:16:58,740 --> 00:17:02,300
 Any object attempting to penetrate the field is pulverized or pushed aside.

208
00:17:02,400 --> 00:17:04,560
 It's deflected, regardless of mass or velocity.

209
00:17:04,560 --> 00:17:10,600
 At the propulsion end, anything approaching would instantly be vaporized.

210
00:17:11,290 --> 00:17:14,410
 There is no means known to propel an object faster than the speed of light.

211
00:17:14,850 --> 00:17:16,450
 such an object would penetrate the shield.

212
00:17:17,150 --> 00:17:19,550
 Therefore, our solution is to approach in this narrow corridor.

213
00:17:19,900 --> 00:17:22,530
 Only a very small yet powerful craft could achieve this.

214
00:17:22,810 --> 00:17:24,310
 Unfortunately, the hummingbird is perfect.

215
00:17:24,530 --> 00:17:25,010
 Then what?

216
00:17:25,600 --> 00:17:28,670
 Piero must land on it and disarm it in time.

217
00:17:29,060 --> 00:17:32,430
 And they should make contact about 14 hours 30, if all goes well.

218
00:17:32,710 --> 00:17:34,990
 They'll have less than half an hour. Is that enough?

219
00:17:35,360 --> 00:17:39,380
 If luck is on our side, he should be able to make a quick entry here,

220
00:17:39,460 --> 00:17:41,120
 and it should lead to the ignition area.

221
00:17:41,120 --> 00:17:45,190
 I think that's true, because this door seems to be the one most used.

222
00:17:45,760 --> 00:17:47,920
 I think they should know that as quickly as possible.

223
00:17:51,070 --> 00:17:54,850
 Calling Hummingbird.

224
00:17:55,410 --> 00:17:56,450
 This is Colonel Pierre.

225
00:17:57,520 --> 00:17:59,860
 Maestro will now give you your final instructions.

226
00:18:00,020 --> 00:18:00,320
 Good luck.

227
00:18:00,560 --> 00:18:05,420
 Yes, well, now, here's what I've been able to piece together from the RIA data.

228
00:18:05,720 --> 00:18:06,740
 Please listen carefully.

229
00:18:07,080 --> 00:18:09,960
 There is only one weak point in the craft's defense, and here's what you do.

230
00:18:15,160 --> 00:18:24,030
 Chief, they don't want to.

231
00:18:24,660 --> 00:18:26,370
 Then we'll blow up the Earth.

232
00:18:26,430 --> 00:18:27,390
 It'll be a good lesson.

233
00:18:27,780 --> 00:18:29,940
 That's what they get for getting in my way.

234
00:18:29,940 --> 00:18:34,140
 Now beyond our control, Admiral.

235
00:18:34,930 --> 00:18:35,920
 Very well.

236
00:18:36,270 --> 00:18:37,110
 Return to base.

237
00:18:47,900 --> 00:19:01,170
 because all communication will be impossible later.

238
00:19:01,310 --> 00:19:04,490
 Jupiter's radiation and the ship's protection shield will block the signals.

239
00:19:05,260 --> 00:19:08,700
 Once you're on the craft, move fast, you'll have under 30 minutes.

240
00:19:08,960 --> 00:19:11,800
 The first 10 minutes, you will pass through the asteroid belt.

241
00:19:11,920 --> 00:19:14,620
 There on the rocket, you'll be protected by its protection shield.

242
00:19:14,920 --> 00:19:18,360
 But be careful, you will also be subjected to fire from our base on Vesta.

243
00:19:18,480 --> 00:19:20,340
 Again, you will be protected by the ship's field.

244
00:19:20,780 --> 00:19:26,060
 The same will happen 15 minutes later when you will be a target for our base on Deimos, near Mars.

245
00:19:26,060 --> 00:19:32,860
 Finally, a few seconds before impact with the Earth, the rocket will be violently attacked by the moon base, but then you should be well away.

246
00:19:33,590 --> 00:19:36,130
 To gain entrance into the rocket itself, don't use lasers.

247
00:19:36,650 --> 00:19:39,810
 They would very likely set off an explosion. Now, you wouldn't want that.

248
00:19:40,270 --> 00:19:45,240
 If for any reason you are unable to enter the craft, leave immediately, preferably before Mars.

249
00:19:46,110 --> 00:19:52,410
 The most critical moment will be when you are leaving the craft, because your escape corridor will be very narrow.

250
00:19:52,870 --> 00:19:58,430
 And the one end, you could disintegrate in the protection shield, and the other be vaporized in the heat of the exhaust.

251
00:19:58,430 --> 00:20:01,590
 Well, that's it. There's nothing more that I can tell you, my friends.

252
00:20:02,630 --> 00:20:08,110
 Oh, yes, your tangent thrust engines must be run up to maximum power to disengage you from the craft.

253
00:20:08,480 --> 00:20:11,160
 Well, we're all with you in spirit.

254
00:20:11,360 --> 00:20:14,890
 We'll try to monitor your radio signals until you're free of the craft.

255
00:20:15,330 --> 00:20:18,840
 Remember, the survival of our way of life is in your hands.

256
00:20:20,640 --> 00:20:38,520
 Engine thrust engines at maximum power.

257
00:20:56,960 --> 00:20:59,010
 Now, magnetic anchors operating.

258
00:21:06,840 --> 00:21:09,660
 Engines have been cut.

259
00:21:48,690 --> 00:21:53,940
 We get it from Vesta.

260
00:21:56,810 --> 00:21:59,920
 No good. We're wasting time.

261
00:21:59,920 --> 00:22:01,750
 We'll each take a look around the ship.

262
00:22:01,980 --> 00:22:03,710
 See if we can find some other way in, okay?

263
00:22:03,990 --> 00:22:06,260
 We'll meet back here at 45 precisely.

264
00:22:18,420 --> 00:22:19,550
 Hummingbird, do you read me?

265
00:22:20,140 --> 00:22:21,180
 This is Omega Control.

266
00:22:21,990 --> 00:22:24,200
 This is Omega Control.

267
00:22:26,660 --> 00:22:29,610
 Control calling Hummingbird.

268
00:22:31,660 --> 00:22:32,820
 Hummingbird, come in.

269
00:22:33,280 --> 00:22:34,700
 This is Omega Control.

270
00:22:38,280 --> 00:22:44,950
 It's like it was one solid block.

271
00:22:45,250 --> 00:22:48,410
 There isn't a crack or a cranny in the whole darn thing.

272
00:22:48,890 --> 00:22:50,460
 And we don't have much time.

273
00:22:51,120 --> 00:22:52,340
 As of now, every minute counts.

274
00:23:01,510 --> 00:23:02,860
 Psyche.

275
00:23:04,710 --> 00:23:22,260
 In case it doesn't work, so long, slumber.

276
00:23:27,350 --> 00:23:39,820
 There's no way.

277
00:23:40,980 --> 00:23:42,660
 This is Omega Control.

278
00:23:42,660 --> 00:23:46,230
 This is Omega Control. Hummingbird, come in.

279
00:23:46,230 --> 00:23:49,400
 I know how we can do it.

280
00:23:49,400 --> 00:23:57,950
 Wish this thing had a rudder to steer it.

281
00:23:57,950 --> 00:24:01,890
 Wait a second. Yes, a rudder to steer it.

282
00:24:01,890 --> 00:24:07,890
 Yes, Psyche, I have a solution too.

283
00:24:07,890 --> 00:24:09,980
 And I bet our two ideas are just the same.

284
00:24:09,980 --> 00:24:12,520
 Quick, back into the ship.

285
00:24:12,520 --> 00:24:28,270
 Engage magnetic anchor.

286
00:24:28,270 --> 00:24:29,910
 Anchor's disengaged.

287
00:24:29,910 --> 00:24:44,170
 Anchor's in hold position.

288
00:24:44,170 --> 00:24:46,150
 Let's hope that they hold.

289
00:24:46,150 --> 00:24:47,660
 Anchor's operating.

290
00:24:47,660 --> 00:24:48,660
 Power on full.

291
00:24:48,660 --> 00:24:51,960
 Mars base is firing.

292
00:24:51,960 --> 00:24:52,860
 Here we go.

293
00:24:52,860 --> 00:25:11,290
 Seem to you that there's a deviation in the trajectory?

294
00:25:11,290 --> 00:25:12,290
 Yes, it is deviating.

295
00:25:12,290 --> 00:25:14,320
 It's changing course. It'll miss Earth.

296
00:25:18,400 --> 00:25:24,750
 Okay now, trajectory is good, now let's get out of here.

297
00:25:25,200 --> 00:25:26,820
 Disengage magnetic anchors.

298
00:25:27,170 --> 00:25:28,740
 Anchors away, Pierro!

299
00:25:29,390 --> 00:25:36,920
 Engine thrust at maximum power.

300
00:25:48,770 --> 00:25:56,480
 Yes, Dad, everything's okay.

301
00:26:02,210 --> 00:26:07,550
 The deadly rocket plunged into the surface of the sun and was swallowed up.

302
00:26:07,550 --> 00:26:11,840
 And the sun went on with his routine terrible violence.

